From: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bsps/riscv/esp32c5: enable SRAM execution before tasks start

The ROM leaves PMA entry 14 mapping SRAM without execute permission. Wi-Fi
initialization used to hide this, but the RTC timecounter and hardware sleep
entry must execute from SRAM even before networking starts. Like ESP-IDF,
allow executable SRAM while retaining the ROM mapping's other attributes.

Signed-off-by: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
---
--- a/bsps/riscv/esp32/start/bspstart.c
+++ b/bsps/riscv/esp32/start/bspstart.c
@@ -264,6 +264,26 @@
 
 void bsp_start( void )
 {
+#if defined( LIBBSP_ESP32_C5_CHIP_DEFINITIONS_H )
+  /* Like ESP-IDF, permit execution from SRAM. The direct-boot ROM leaves
+   * PMA entry 14 read/write only, which also constrains machine mode.
+   * Keep its range and other attributes, adding only execute permission.
+   */
+  uint32_t sram_pma;
+  __asm__ volatile (
+    ".option push\n"
+    ".option arch, +zicsr\n"
+    "csrr %0, 0xbce\n"
+    "csrw 0xbce, zero\n"
+    "ori %0, %0, 4\n"
+    "csrw 0xbce, %0\n"
+    ".option pop\n"
+    : "=&r" ( sram_pma )
+    :
+    : "memory"
+  );
+#endif
+
 #if defined( LIBBSP_ESP32_S31_CHIP_DEFINITIONS_H )
   bsp_esp32s31_initialize_pma();
 #endif
